Subject: chimera: release 1.4 draws the copy protection table when a game starts

SDLPoP draws the copy protection table in every start_game(), so once at
power-on (before the title) and again when a key on the title starts the
game. That is release 1.0's program, which SDLPoP is. Prince of Persia 1.4
on DOS draws it once, when the game starts: at power-on it has drawn one
random number (init_game_main) and nothing else until a key is pressed.
Measured on the DOS game under DOSBox-X: seed 000CBE2A from the clock,
9D018C45 after start-up, unchanged through the title, then the table and
two more draws when Enter is pressed.

Under CHIMERA_CORE, when the release played is 1.4 (chimera_release()), the
table is drawn only when a game is about to start. The other releases were
not measured and keep SDLPoP's behaviour.

--- a/src/seg000.c
+++ b/src/seg000.c
@@ -209,6 +209,10 @@
 	release_title_images(); // added
 	free_optsnd_chtab(); // added
 #ifdef USE_COPYPROT
+#ifdef CHIMERA_CORE
+	// Release 1.4 draws the table when a game starts, not when the title comes up.
+	if (chimera_release() != 14 || start_level >= 0 || custom->skip_title) {
+#endif
 	copyprot_plac = prandom(13);
 	memset(&entry_used, 0, sizeof(entry_used));
 	memset(&letts_used, 0, sizeof(letts_used));
@@ -224,6 +228,9 @@
 		entry_used[which_entry] = 1;
 		letts_used[copyprot_letter[which_entry]-'A'] = 1;
 	}
+#ifdef CHIMERA_CORE
+	}
+#endif
 #endif
 	if (custom->skip_title) { // CusPop option: skip the title sequence (level loads instantly)
 		int level_number = (start_level >= 0) ? start_level : custom->first_level;
